          "identifier": "D",
          "content": "Cr<sup>2+</sup> &gt; Ru<sup>3+</sup> &gt; Fe<sup>2+</sup> &gt; V<sup>2+</sup>"
        }
      ],
      "correct_options": [
        "B"
      ],
      "explanation": "<picture><source media=\"(max-width: 320px)\" srcset=\"https://imagex.cdn.examgoal.net/7km5fk0l7sc8e/bae58e0d-dc37-43b5-b07a-490b7382274f/bdf700e0-d7d8-11e9-acf6-6d09a288f7f2/file-7km5fk0l7sc8f-320w.jpg\"><img src=\"https://imagex.cdn.examgoal.net/7km5fk0l7sc8e/bae58e0d-dc37-43b5-b07a-490b7382274f/bdf700e0-d7d8-11e9-acf6-6d09a288f7f2/file-7km5fk0l7sc8f-500w.jpg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;height: auto;display: block;margin: 0 auto;\" loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"JEE Main 2019 (Online) 8th April Morning Slot Chemistry - Coordination Compounds Question 290 English Explanation 1\"></picture>\n<br>Here number of unpaired electrons = 3\n<br><br><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.186ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.509ex\" height=\"1.251ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -471 667 553\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"2234\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2234\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> Spin only magnetic moment (<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.489ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.364ex\" height=\"1.489ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -442 603 658\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D707\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D707\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>) = <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.639ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"17.814ex\" height=\"2.851ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -977.5 7873.7 1260\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msqrt\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(0,67.5)\"><use data-c=\"221A\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-SO-221A\"></use></g><g transform=\"translate(1020,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mn\"><use data-c=\"33\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-33\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mrow\" transform=\"translate(666.7,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"28\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-28\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\" transform=\"translate(389,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mn\"><use data-c=\"33\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-33\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(722.2,0)\"><use data-c=\"2B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(1722.4,0)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(2611.4,0)\"><use data-c=\"29\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-29\"></use></g></g></g><rect width=\"3667.1\" height=\"60\" x=\"1020\" y=\"857.5\"></rect></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(4964.9,0)\"><use data-c=\"3D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-3D\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"msqrt\" transform=\"translate(6020.7,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(0,89.5)\"><use data-c=\"221A\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-221A\"></use></g><g transform=\"translate(853,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mn\"><use data-c=\"31\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-31\"></use><use data-c=\"35\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-35\" transform=\"translate(500,0)\"></use></g></g><rect width=\"1000\" height=\"60\" x=\"853\" y=\"829.5\"></rect></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> B.M\n<br><br><b>Note : </b> Energy of t<sub>2g</sub> is less than e<sub>g</sub>. As electrons always go to the lower energy level orbitals first, that is why electrons goes to the t<sub>2g</sub> orbital first.\n<picture><source media=\"(max-width: 320px)\" srcset=\"https://imagex.cdn.examgoal.net/7km5fk0l9zv8y/9585b343-6616-4ddd-bf3f-bbfa33479881/61937d20-d7e1-11e9-acf6-6d09a288f7f2/file-7km5fk0l9zv8z-320w.jpg\"><img src=\"https://imagex.cdn.examgoal.net/7km5fk0l9zv8y/9585b343-6616-4ddd-bf3f-bbfa33479881/61937d20-d7e1-11e9-acf6-6d09a288f7f2/file-7km5fk0l9zv8z-500w.jpg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;height: auto;display: block;margin: 0 auto;\" loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"JEE Main 2019 (Online) 8th April Morning Slot Chemistry - Coordination Compounds Question 290 English Explanation 2\"></picture>\n<br>Here number of unpaired electrons = 0\n<br><br><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.186ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.509ex\" height=\"1.251ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -471 667 553\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"2234\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2234\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> Spin only magnetic moment (<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.489ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.364ex\" height=\"1.489ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -442 603 658\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D707\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D707\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>) = 0 B.M\n<br><br><b>Note :</b> (1) As CN<sup>-</sup> is a strong field ligand so Energy gap between e<sub>g</sub> and t<sub>2g</sub> orbital is very high.\n<br><br>(2) [Fe(CN)<sub>6</sub>]<sup>4–</sup> is an octahedral complex. And for octahedral complex  Energy gap between e<sub>g</sub> and t<sub>2g</sub> orbital is called <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: 0;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.885ex\" height=\"1.62ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -716 833 716\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"394\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-394\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container><sub>0</sub> or Crystal Field splitting Energy.\n<br><br>(3) Energy required to pair up the electron in same orbital is called Pairing Energy(P).\n<br><br>(4) For strong field ligand, <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: 0;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.885ex\" height=\"1.62ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -716 833 716\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"394\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-394\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container><sub>0</sub> is very high and for weak field ligand, <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: 0;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.885ex\" height=\"1.62ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -716 833 716\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"394\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-394\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container><sub>0</sub> is very low.\n<br><br>(5) For strong field ligand, <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: 0;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.885ex\" height=\"1.62ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -716 833 716\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"394\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-394\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container><sub>0</sub> &gt; P, so when electron gets energy, pairing of electrons happens as for pairing of electrons very low energy requied.\n<br><br>(6) For weak field ligand, <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: 0;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.885ex\" height=\"1.62ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -716 833 716\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"394\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-394\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container><sub>0</sub> &lt; P, so when electron gets energy, pairing of electrons does not happens as the energy required to enter into the e<sub>g</sub> orbital is less than pairing energy. That is why electron go to e<sub>g</sub> orbital first.\n<br><br>(7) As CN<sup>-</sup> is a strong field ligand so pairing of electron occurs.\n<picture><source media=\"(max-width: 320px)\" srcset=\"https://imagex.cdn.examgoal.net/7km5fk0lv9hk6/81c3c35c-a843-4d8d-b082-d70eec7ff976/8cce4c60-d834-11e9-acf6-6d09a288f7f2/file-7km5fk0lv9hk7-320w.jpg\"><img src=\"https://imagex.cdn.examgoal.net/7km5fk0lv9hk6/81c3c35c-a843-4d8d-b082-d70eec7ff976/8cce4c60-d834-11e9-acf6-6d09a288f7f2/file-7km5fk0lv9hk7-500w.jpg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;height: auto;display: block;margin: 0 auto;\" loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"JEE Main 2019 (Online) 8th April Morning Slot Chemistry - Coordination Compounds Question 290 English Explanation 3\"></picture>\n<br>Here number of unpaired electrons = 1\n<br><br><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.186ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.509ex\" height=\"1.251ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -471 667 553\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"2234\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2234\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> Spin only magnetic moment (<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.489ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.364ex\" height=\"1.489ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -442 603 658\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D707\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D707\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>) = <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.639ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16.683ex\" height=\"2.851ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -977.5 7373.7 1260\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msqrt\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(0,67.5)\"><use data-c=\"221A\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-SO-221A\"></use></g><g transform=\"translate(1020,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mn\"><use data-c=\"31\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-31\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mrow\" transform=\"translate(666.7,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"28\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-28\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\" transform=\"translate(389,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mn\"><use data-c=\"31\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-31\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(722.2,0)\"><use data-c=\"2B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(1722.4,0)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(2611.4,0)\"><use data-c=\"29\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-29\"></use></g></g></g><rect width=\"3667.1\" height=\"60\" x=\"1020\" y=\"857.5\"></rect></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(4964.9,0)\"><use data-c=\"3D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-3D\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"msqrt\" transform=\"translate(6020.7,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(0,89)\"><use data-c=\"221A\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-221A\"></use></g><g transform=\"translate(853,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mn\"><use data-c=\"33\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-33\"></use></g></g><rect width=\"500\" height=\"60\" x=\"853\" y=\"829\"></rect></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> B.M\n<br><br><b>Note :</b> (1) In [Ru(NH<sub>3</sub>)<sub>6</sub>]<sup>3+</sup> complex, NH<sub>3</sub> is a strong field ligand so Energy gap between e<sub>g</sub> and t<sub>2g</sub> orbital is very high. That is why pairing of electrons occurs.\n<picture><source media=\"(max-width: 320px)\" srcset=\"https://imagex.cdn.examgoal.net/7km5fk0lvh47o/3d1d7276-5034-4011-8849-aa09c4de4f38/60f7f540-d835-11e9-acf6-6d09a288f7f2/file-7km5fk0lvh47p-320w.jpg\"><img src=\"https://imagex.cdn.examgoal.net/7km5fk0lvh47o/3d1d7276-5034-4011-8849-aa09c4de4f38/60f7f540-d835-11e9-acf6-6d09a288f7f2/file-7km5fk0lvh47p-500w.jpg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;height: auto;display: block;margin: 0 auto;\" loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"JEE Main 2019 (Online) 8th April Morning Slot Chemistry - Coordination Compounds Question 290 English Explanation 4\"></picture>\n<br>Here number of unpaired electrons = 2\n<br><br><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: